summary:
  An answer that named only the listener's own stations counts as empty.

history:
  What an empty answer tries next was told by the web rows alone. Saved
  stations an answer names are shown in the list and left out of the web
  rows, so a genre page of fifty of them read as nothing found: the word
  was shaved to its stem and asked again as a name ("techno" as "techn"),
  or the country chip was dropped and the text run again everywhere. They
  are counted as found.

target:
  package/contents/ui/SearchLogic.js

find:
      var found = n(s.count) + n(s.own);

replace:
      var found = n(s.count);

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_searchlogic.qml::test_saved_stations_an_answer_named_are_no_empty_answer
  and tests/qml/tst_searchlogic.qml::test_a_thin_answer_counts_the_listeners_own_stations_too.
  Line-neutral.
